#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Fixture CLI for the classic `gz` tool. Recorded from Classic 11.15.1 (conda env
# solus-gz-classic) on 2026-11-09 against a headless `gzserver empty.world` the recording script
# started and terminated through its own Popen handle, with a two-link URDF spawned as `twolink`.
# `gz --version` / `gz sim --versions` print "Invalid arguments" on STDERR and exit 255, so the
# detector never reads a classic install as the new family. The `goo.gle/debug*` marker lines are
# what the conda protobuf build prints before every DebugString and are kept verbatim.
# Re-recorded live in P8-T2 (2026-11-09, docs/qa/acceptance/P8-live-smoke.md): `topic -e ... -d`
# takes WHOLE seconds — `-d 0.3` / `-d 1.0` print "Invalid arguments" on stderr and exit 0 with
# no stdout; `-d 1` echoes ~5 world_stats messages (one per 0.2 s) in ~1.2 s.
# `model -w <w> -m broken -f <file> ...` replays a URDF the parser rejects (recorded live in
# P8-T2 (2026-11-09) and again in P9-T3: rc 0, stdout empty, the `Error:` lines below on
# stderr; `model -m broken -i` then prints "Unable to get info on model[broken] in the
# world[default]" on STDOUT with rc 0 — P8 defect B).
# Knob: GZ_PARTITION=solus-fixture-paused → world_stats says `paused: true` (only env.allow names
# cross the adapters' scrubbed child environment, so the test selects the replay that way).
# Knob: GZ_PARTITION=solus-fixture-nonfinite → `angle: nan` / `angle: inf` in the model info
# (AUTHORED from protobuf's DebugString float printing; what diverged physics reports).
# Knob: GZ_PARTITION=solus-fixture-idle → `topic -l` lists no `/gazebo/<world>/...` topic
# (AUTHORED: the listing before any gzserver is up).
